+# Change record: Ambiguous: 'make it safer and give marketing better insight'
+
+_Run `ambiguous`. Generated by the docs agent._
+
+## Requirement (as stated)
+
+> Make our link shortener safer for the people who click our links, and give marketing better insight into how their links perform.
+
+## Interpreted as
+
+- **Create short links** (stated (matched 'shorten'))
+  - FR-1: A client can submit an absolute http(s) URL and receive a unique, non-guessable short code and short URL.
+  - FR-2: Invalid, unsafe or self-referencing destination URLs are rejected with a validation error.
+- **Click analytics** (stated (matched 'click'))
+  - FR-3: Link owners can see total clicks, clicks per day and top referrers for a link.
+- **Block known-malicious destinations** (clarification AMB-safety=denylist)
+  - FR-4: Operators can configure a denylist of destination domains (including their subdomains); links to them cannot be created.
+- **Per-country click analytics** (clarification AMB-insight=geo)
+  - FR-5: Click analytics include a per-country breakdown.
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Protect the service: only authenticated clients (API keys) may create links (not chosen for AMB-safety)
+- Traffic sources and daily trends (referrers, clicks per day) (not chosen for AMB-insight)
+
+## Plan
+
+- `T-denylist` Denylist-aware URL validator
+- `T-denylist-wiring` Wire denylist from SHORTENER_BLOCKED_HOSTS (after ["T-denylist"])
+- reused existing: link_creation
+- reused existing: click_analytics
+- excluded: geo_analytics - privacy-review rejected by dpo.office: Per-country analytics needs client IP processing; not allowed without a DPIA. Defer geo analytics; existing referrer and daily-trend analytics remain.
+
+## API changes
+
+- POST /api/v1/links: may now return 400 validation_failed for denylisted hosts (same error shape)
+
+## Risks
+
+- destination_denylist: static denylist goes stale; a reputation feed would be a follow-up
+- destination_denylist: existing links to newly blocked domains keep working (scope decision)
